# The build context is uploaded to Cloud Build, so this file controls both image
# size and what leaves this machine.

# SECRETS. `.env` holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY. They belong in
# Secret Manager, mounted as env vars at deploy time — never in a layer, where
# anyone who can pull the image can read them.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# The 100 MB database is regenerated inside the image, so it stays out. But
# `data/cache/` MUST go in: it holds the three Overpass/OpenStreetMap responses
# (748 KB) that the datagen builds the road network from, and `osm.py` never
# re-fetches a cached file.
#
# Excluding all of `data/` is what broke the first Cloud Build — the datagen
# fell through to a live Overpass call and got `0 elements` back from a flaky
# mirror. Shipping the cache also pins the deployed world to the same road
# network the demo was developed against, instead of whatever Overpass happens
# to return on build day.
data/*
!data/cache

# Rebuilt in the `web` stage. Copying the local one risks deploying a stale bundle.
web/dist/
web/node_modules/

# Logs and scratch — `var/` is where dev/serve.sh and dev/web.sh append.
var/
*.log

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store

# Not needed at runtime.
docs/
dev/
